  "notes": "Modified cash basis city. Governmental beginning/ending are the total governmental funds fund balances (601,215 / 807,151) that the p5 statement rolls forward; they include due from other funds 235,000 and notes receivable 74,232 (cash alone is 560,325 + 11,718 + 108 per p4). Transfers_in 139,527 = net transfers from the utilities fund (General 52,126, Golf 54,799, Housing 2, Street 32,600); utilities side shows (139,527) on p3, p7 and p8. Business-type: lines and balances come from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7, report p11, Utilities Fund; added by the v8 re-trim), accrual, measure net position: 1,803,774 + 511,360 - 451,893 (incl. depreciation 82,701) - 139,527 transfers = 1,723,714. This replaces the earlier figures taken from the modified cash Statement of Activities (p2-3: charges 503,403, expenses 627,699 incl. capital purchases 270,360) and the cash roll-forward 80,415 -> 62,682 (cash flow p8, incl. 235,000 due to other funds), which were used only because p7 was not trimmed. The p6 proprietary Statement of Net Position (accrual, net position 1,723,714, ties to p7) differs from the government-wide modified cash column and was not used for balance_sheet. Detail left empty: the only schedule (p9 Budgetary Comparison - All Funds) mixes governmental, utilities and nursing home (7,652,819 nursing home charges not in these statements) in single lines, so fund types cannot be separated; the statement lines already carry the actuals. Transfer cross-check done: governmental net transfer ties to utilities outflow. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
